} \\\\ & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThere is a pivot for each variable and no contradictory row. The system has a unique solution, so we conclude that the system is consistent independent.\n\nAs a result, only statement II is true." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186523112 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186523154 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186523112 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186523175 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186523112 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186523179 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186523112 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186523112 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y-2z &=-4 \\\\ x+3y &=-8 \\\\ x+y-4z &=-3\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The system is consistent independent\n- **II.** The system is consistent dependent\n- **III.** The system is inconsistent" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186523112 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "2c37a8ce-9961-58b3-83eb-74946c8f3663" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186523112 #edb/ref 1074 "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -2 & -4 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 0 & -8 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -4 & -3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -2 & -4 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 0 & -8 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -4 & -3\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\ & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -4 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -4 & -3\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\ & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(1){R}_{2} \\\\ & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -3\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe final row corresponds to the equation $0x+0y+0z=-3,$ and this has no solution. Therefore, our system has no solution, and we conclude that the system is inconsistent.\n\nAs a result, only statement III is true." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186523119 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186523106 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186523119 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186523144 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186523119 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186523177 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186523119 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186523119 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-3y &=-5 \\\\ -2x+6y &=10\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The system is consistent dependent\n- **II.** The system is consistent independent\n- **III.** The system is inconsistent" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186523119 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "482e6d01-f9bf-525e-86f9-c527dca5de7f" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186523119 #edb/ref 1074 "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & -5 \\\\ -2 & 6 & 10\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & -5 \\\\ -2 & 6 & 10\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(2){R}_{1} \\\\ & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. Here there is one free variable, $y$. Therefore, since there are infinitely many solutions, we conclude that the system is *consistent dependent*.\n\nAs a result, only statement I is true." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186523120 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186523109 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186523120 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186523114 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186523120 