45486 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186523134 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+y+z &=5 \\\\ x+2y+2z &=7 \\\\ x+3y+5z &=8\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The system is consistent dependent\n- **II.** The system is consistent independent\n- **III.** The system is inconsistent" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186523134 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "636c60f0-5dc2-592a-9ada-f299790fa243" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186523134 #edb/ref 1074 "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 2 & 7 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 5 & 8\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 2 & 7 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 5 & 8\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\ & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 5 & 8\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\ & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 4 & 3\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{2} \\\\ & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThere is a pivot for each variable and no contradictory row. The system has a unique solution, so we conclude that the system is consistent independent.\n\nAs a result, only statement II is true." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186523146 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186523156 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186523146 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186523173 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186523146 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186523185 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186523146 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186523146 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y-z &=1 \\\\ 2x+5y &=7 \\\\ -2x-3y+5z &=6\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The system is inconsistent\n- **II.** The system is consistent independent\n- **III.** The system is consistent dependent" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186523146 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "8a8ea6cd-37c6-57a9-b6bb-655208ae0dae" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186523146 #edb/ref 1074 "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 5 & 0 & 7 \\\\ -2 & -3 & 5 & 6\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 5 & 0 & 7 \\\\ -2 & -3 & 5 & 6\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\ & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 5 \\\\ -2 & -3 & 5 & 6\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(2){R}_{1} \\\\ & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 8\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{2} \\\\ & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThere is a pivot for each variable and no contradictory row. The system has a unique solution, so we conclude that the system is consistent independent.\n\nAs a result, only statement II is true." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186523149 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186523097 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186523149 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186523145 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186523149 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186523155 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186523149 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186523149 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+y &=1 \\\\ 2x+4y &=4\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect 