\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 4 \\\\ -1 & 0 & -8\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(1){R}_{1} \\\\ & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThere is a pivot for each variable and no contradictory row. The system has a unique solution, so we conclude that the system is consistent independent.\n\nAs a result, only statement II is true." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186523181 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186523104 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186523181 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186523115 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186523181 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186523168 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186523181 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186523181 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-3y-3z &=5 \\\\ 2x-5y-9z &=10 \\\\ 2x-5y-9z &=10\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The system is consistent dependent\n- **II.** The system is inconsistent\n- **III.** The system is consistent independent" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186523181 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ec9855f3-8df8-5de8-aa96-4a294a867b64" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186523181 #edb/ref 1074 "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & -3 & 5 \\\\ 2 & -5 & -9 & 10 \\\\ 2 & -5 & -9 & 10\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & -3 & 5 \\\\ 2 & -5 & -9 & 10 \\\\ 2 & -5 & -9 & 10\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\ & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & -3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -5 & -9 & 10\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\ & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & -3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & 0\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{2} \\\\ & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & -3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. Here there is one free variable, $z$. Therefore, since there are infinitely many solutions, we conclude that the system is *consistent dependent*.\n\nAs a result, only statement I is true." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186523190 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186523093 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186523190 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186523172 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186523190 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186523180 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186523190 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186523190 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y &=-3 \\\\ -2x-4y &=3\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The system is consistent independent\n- **II.** The system is consistent dependent\n- **III.** The system is inconsistent" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186523190 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "fe67b029-391e-51be-a295-1e535d93c516" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186523190 #edb/ref 1074 "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ -2 & -4 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ -2 & -4 & 3\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(2){R}_{1} \\\\ & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe final row corresponds to the equation $0x+0y=-3,$ and this has no solution. Therefore, our system has no solution, and we conclude that the system is inconsistent.\n\nAs a result, only statement III is true." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186523192 #edb/ref 1168 "generate/scratch/17592186115299.py" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186523192 #edb/ref 1169 #uuid "ef6ae15d-64a0-50e2-9946-0e7f859493c2" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186557414 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186557436 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186557414 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186557414 #edb/ref 1071 "Determine the value of $k$ for which the following system of linear equations is inconsistent:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+3y &=-5 \\\\ 2x+ky &=-8\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186557414 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "2d5b5966-d0b2-51ba-a7a1-c76ebe8e6658" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186557414 #edb/ref 1074 "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 3 & -5 \\\\ 2 & k & -8\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 3 & -5 \\\\ 2 & k & -8\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 3 & -5 \\\\ 0 & k-6 & 2\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+3y &=-5 \\\\ (k-6)y &=2.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe system is inconsistent if it has no solutions. For the system to have no solutions, one of the equations above must be false.\n\nIf $k=6,$ then the second equation is $0=2,$ which is false, and the system will have no solution.\n\nTherefore, our system is inconsistent when $k=6.$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186557415 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186557422 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186557415 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186557415 #edb/ref 1071 "Determine the value of $k$ for which the following system of linear equations is inconsistent:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y &=-4 \\\\ -2x+ky &=5\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186557415 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "364e838c-b667-5333-9687-aeee90961e0c" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186557415 #edb/ref 1074 "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 2 & -4 \\\\ -2 & k & 5\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 2 & -4 \\\\ -2 & k & 5\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & k+4 & -3\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y &=-4 \\\\ (k+4)y &=-3.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe system is inconsistent if it has no solutions. For the system to have no solutions, one of the equations above must be false.\n\nIf $k=-4,$ then the second equation is $0=-3,$ which is false, and the system will have no solution.\n\nTherefore, our system is inconsistent when $k=-4.$" #edb/ref 17592186045443]}
